's how the regex works:\n\n**Key Components:**\n\n1. **IPv4 Address Detection** - `(?=.*\\b(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4]\\d|1\\d{2}|[1-9]?\\d)\\.(...)\\b)`\n   - Lookahead ensures the line contains a valid IPv4 address\n   - Each octet pattern matches 0-255 without leading zeros\n\n2. **Greedy Match to Last Date** - `.*`\n   - Greedily matches everything, forcing the regex to find the rightmost valid date\n\n3. **Date Pattern with Month/Day Constraints**:\n   - **31-day months** (01,03,05,07,08,10,12): `(?:0[13578]|1[02])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])`\n   - **30-day months** (04,06,09,11): `(?:0[469]|11)-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|30)`\n   - **February** (up to 29 days): `02-(?:0[1-9]|1\\d|2[0-9])`\n\n4. **Word Boundaries** - `(?<![A-Za-z0-9-])` and `(?![A-Za-z0-9-])`\n   - Prevents false matches like \"1134-12-1234\" or \"text2024-01-15text\"\n\nWhen used with `re.findall()` and `re.MULTILINE`, this will extract only the last valid date from each line that contains an IPv4 address.","ttft_ms":95925,"type":"result","duration_ms":101990,"uuid":"e87ea0f7-5763-41b9-8c7c-c46262d71e28","ttft_stream_ms":654,"time_to_request_ms":71,"queued_turn_count":0}
